An Azure governance baseline establishes a minimum set of standards that every cloud environment should follow before workloads are deployed.

A governance baseline may define requirements for:

* Identity and access
* Resource naming
* Resource tagging
* Allowed regions
* Network security
* Logging and monitoring
* Backup
* Cost management
* Compliance

For example, an enterprise may require every production resource to have an owner tag, approved region, monitoring configuration, appropriate RBAC assignments, and defined backup requirements.

A real-life use case is a company onboarding multiple development teams to Azure while ensuring that every team follows the same minimum governance requirements.

A strong governance baseline provides a repeatable foundation for secure, manageable, and cost-effective Azure adoption.
